---
description: Use the cresa.one plugin skills and the OAuth MCP server for Sites and Drives. Never paste API keys.
alwaysApply: true
---

cresa.one: for publishing, access, domains, Site Data, or Drives, follow the bundled cresa-one skills. On a new install, follow the setup skill: state what the connection can read, change, and send, sign in with the emailed code, publish one welcome Site, then update that same URL. Live calls use the remote MCP server and OAuth. Do not paste API keys, Drive tokens, or client secrets into chat or into plugin files. For the person's own files, ask for an offline dry run before the first upload. Use the show_site tool when a host can show the Site card, with onboarding set on a first run.
